messages:
nina: Heads-up — mobile sample apps are inconsistent with server/desktop SDKs for error shapes. iOS surface uses NSError with domain string and codes, Android uses HttpException with no structured payload, Flutter returns PlatformException. This breaks the onboarding snippet where we show catching RateLimit and showing retry UI.

kevin: Yikes. Which endpoints do we care most about? Streaming chat on mobile or sync generate?

nina: Both, but streaming is worse because partial content is valuable on mobile UX. Example: Android recent crash report showed app blindly parsing plaintext and crashing when trying to extract retry_after.

rachel: We should define a mobile-friendly normalization layer: server returns the error envelope (same as desktop): `{\"error\":{\"message\":\"Quota exceeded\",\"code\":\"rate_limit\",\"retry_after_ms\":1200,\"retryable\":true,\"meta\":{}}}`. SDKs then map this to platform idioms: Swift -> NSError with userInfo keys `code`, `retry_after_ms`, `retryable`; Kotlin -> subclassed exceptions `RateLimitException(retryAfterMs=1200)`, Flutter -> custom `ApiException` with fields.

kevin: For Swift example catching pattern we'd want something like:
```swift
do {
  try client.generate(...)
} catch let err as RateLimitError {
  showRetryUI(afterMs: err.retryAfterMs)
} catch {
  showGenericError()
}
```
And for Kotlin:
```kotlin
try {
  client.generate(...)
} catch (e: RateLimitException) {
  scheduleRetry(e.retryAfterMs)
}
```

nina: Exactly. Also need a plan for legacy flows: many mobile apps pin older SDKs. So SDKs should implement a `normalizeErrors` boolean (opt-in) in the minor release; default false, flip in next major. When true, adapter normalizes legacy plaintext/HTML/old-json into the exceptions above.

rachel: Streaming UX: mobile libs should emit `onError(error: ApiError, partial: String?)` where `partial` is any delivered text. On iOS that could be a delegate method, on Android a callback. Having partial lets apps show partial reply rather than nothing.

kevin: Good point — also add `idempotency_key` handling for safe retries on client side. If server returns `retryable: true` we should include guidance for mobile SDKs to re-run with the same idempotency key. Include `last_token_index` in meta for streaming so apps can resume.

nina: UX note: message MUST be safe for end users. Put traces/request_id/model into `meta` not in `message`. Add `retry_after_ms` and also provide `retryable` boolean. Example final envelope we require from server:
```json
{\"error\":{
  \"message\":\"Rate limit exceeded\",
  \"code\":\"rate_limit\",
  \"retry_after_ms\":1500,
  \"retryable\":true,
  \"meta\":{\"request_id\":\"r-123\",\"model\":\"gpt-x\"}
}}
```

rachel: Implementation owners? I can take iOS (Swift) normalization + sampleapp update. Kevin can do Android + Kotlin exceptions. Nina will own Flutter adapter and the mobile sampleapps test harness.

kevin: I'll add typed exception classes and a NormalizeError(resp) helper in Kotlin. Will add unit tests and an e2e in mobile-samples that asserts same exception mapping as Node/Python. ETA next Tue.

nina: I'll add a tiny fixture server in mobile-samples/test-fixtures that toggles legacy/plaintext vs envelope responses and also emits a streaming partial+terminal-error scenario. Will add CI job that runs Swift/Kotlin/Flutter sampleapps and asserts parity. ETA EOW.

rachel: iOS plan: wrap server errors into `ApiError: Error` protocol with concrete `RateLimitError` struct that also sets underlying NSError for Objective-C interop. Add docs snippet for `catch let err as RateLimitError` and fallback using `err.code`. ETA next Wed.

mobile-ci: Created ticket INFR-2044: \"mobile SDK error normalization + sampleapp parity (iOS/Android/Flutter)\" assigned to rachel,kevin,nina. https://redwood.atlassian.com/browse/INFR-2044

kevin: Small compatibility caveat: for Swift/ObjC bridging, keep NSError domain and integer code stable. Populate userInfo with `ApiErrorCode` and `RetryAfterMs` keys. Avoid changing ObjC-visible types in patch releases.

nina: Also add a short docs page \"Mobile SDK: Error shapes & handling\" with code snippets for Swift/Kotlin/Flutter showing both class-catch and checking `error.code` string. I'll stub and send to docs for copy edit.

rachel: One more thing: include a tiny troubleshooting checklist in the doc: common failure modes (plaintext body, HTML error page from proxy, missing retry_after). Show how NormalizeError handles them.

kevin: Sounds good. We'll sync progress in mobile guild on Friday. Thanks all. :thumbsup:
